Suggested fixes
  1. Menus do not depend on hover [hover-only-menus, weight 3]
     Expose submenus through a <button aria-expanded> toggle, or render submenu links in the
     page (footer sitemap) so they are reachable without hover.
  2. Structured data (JSON-LD) describes the page [structured-data, weight 3]
     Add JSON-LD for Organization/WebSite on the home page and Product/Offer, FAQPage,
     ContactPoint or BreadcrumbList on inner pages.
  3. Targets are large enough [target-size, weight 1]
     Make interactive targets at least 24×24 CSS px with spacing.
  4. No runtime errors during load [console-errors, weight 3]
     Fix uncaught exceptions and failed script requests reported during load.
  5. Control names are specific, not repeated or generic [ambiguous-control-names, weight 3]
     Make link and button text describe the destination or action ("Read the return policy",
     "Add Trail Bike to cart"). Avoid "Click here"/"Read more"; use aria-label to disambiguate
     when visual text must stay short.
  6. Common destinations are discoverable from the start page [key-pages-discoverable, weight 3]
     Link contact, help/FAQ, privacy/terms, and search from the header or footer with their
     conventional names.
  7. llms.txt is published and well-formed [llms-txt, weight 3]
     Publish /llms.txt with an H1, a one-paragraph blockquote and H2 sections of markdown links
     to the most useful pages.
  8. Site search is exposed [search-available, weight 1]
     Expose search as <form role="search"> with a labelled <input type="search">, and declare a
     SearchAction in WebSite JSON-LD.

